<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to pay $202 mln to Paris Club.</title>
<headline>Brazil to pay $202 mln to Paris Club.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil will pay Friday $202.35 million in principal and interest to the Paris Club of creditor nations, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement it would pay $60.269 million to Japan, $43.453 million to France and $23.155 million to Germany.</p>
<p>It would also pay $22.229 million to the United States, $20.563 to Britain and $17.274 million to Italy.</p>
<p>The rest will be divided among the other Paris Club members.</p>
<p>Of the total, $192.56 million refers to principal and $9.79 million to interest.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-3141193))</p>
